    "note": "The first wave produced 3269 distinct names for 3404 bindings and only 112 of them appear in more than one file: the vocabulary is mostly one-off domain nouns, so a closed list would reject the whole corpus and teach nothing. What this gate enforces is therefore layered: HARD = no compressed name, no word+digits shape, no banned disambiguator, no collision, no two names for one binding; SOFT (warning) = a name the glossary has never seen, reported with the canonicals its words suggest.",
